```gitignore
# Dependencies
/node_modules
yarn-error.log*

# Build output
/ios/build
/android/app/build
/android/.gradle
*.xcworkspace # Ignore workspace files that might contain build artifacts
/Podfile.lock # Sometimes useful but if other people update pods, we want to regenerate it sometimes. However, generally better to keep it unless explicitly instructed otherwise. Let's exclude build specific outputs instead.

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Snapshots*

# Logs and temporary data
npm-debug.log-*
yarn-error.log*
*.swp

# Metro Bundler cache directory (usually found in the project root or android/app/.cache)
# It's safer to ignore specific directories if they appear, but usually just letting node_modules/ and build outputs handle it is fine. A dedicated one:
node_modules/.cache/
metro-cache/

# Testing/Linting/Coverage reports (if generated during CI or local runs)
coverage/
__mocks__/

# Platform Specifics (These are generally already covered, but good to keep explicit)
android/local.properties # Highly sensitive file containing local machine paths
android/.idea/ # Android Studio files
ios/Pods/ # Should be managed by pod install, but sometimes build artifacts land here.
```